      "content": "that's a lot of specific downsides for the economy... but what about the downsides of NOT intervening? like, if we don't do anything, isn't it basically a given that small competitors will just get crushed and there won't be any real innovation left anyway? feels like the 'innovation' argument might just be a way to protect their margins.",
